In trapezoid $ABCD$, the sides $AB$ and $CD$ are equal. What is the perimeter of $ABCD$? [asy]
/* AMC8 1999 #14 Problem */
pen p = linetype("4 4");
draw((0,0)--(4,3)--(12,3)--(16,0)--cycle);
draw((4,0)--(4,3), p);
draw((3.5,0)--(3.5, .5)--(4.0,0.5));

label(scale(0.75)*"A", (0,0), W);
label(scale(0.75)*"B", (4,3), NW);
label(scale(0.75)*"C", (12, 3), NE);
label(scale(0.75)*"D", (16, 0), E);
label(scale(0.75)*"8", (8,3), N);
label(scale(0.75)*"16", (8,0), S);
label(scale(0.75)*"3", (4, 1.5), E);
[/asy]

Square $ABCD$ is constructed along diameter $AB$ of a semicircle, as shown. The semicircle and square $ABCD$ are coplanar. Line segment $AB$ has a length of 6 centimeters. If point $M$ is the midpoint of arc $AB$, what is the length of segment $MC$? Express your answer in simplest radical form. [asy]
size(4cm);

dotfactor = 4;
defaultpen(linewidth(1)+fontsize(10pt));

pair A,B,C,D,M;
A = (0,1);
B = (1,1);
C = (1,0);
D = (0,0);
M = (.5,1.5);

draw(A..M..B--C--D--cycle);
draw(A--B);

dot("A",A,W);
dot("M",M,N);
dot("B",B,E);
dot("C",C,E);
dot("D",D,W);

draw(M--C,linetype("0 4"));

[/asy]

The smaller square in the figure below has a perimeter of $4$ cm, and the larger square has an area of $16$ $\text{cm}^2$.  What is the distance from point $A$ to point $B$? Express your answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth.

[asy]
draw((0,0)--(12,0));
draw((2,0)--(2,10));
draw((0,0)--(0,2));
draw((0,2)--(2,2));
draw((0,2)--(12,10));
draw((12,0)--(12,10));
draw((2,10)--(12,10));
label("B",(0,2),W);
label("A",(12,10),E);
[/asy]
